<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41697" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhŏdŏpē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥοδόπη.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A mountain range in Thrace</i>, <i>a
				part of the Hæmus</i>, now <i>Despoto
				Dagh</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 2, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 3,
				351</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2, 222</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10,
			77</span></i>.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Acc. to the myth, originally a man,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 6, 87 sq.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>Thrace</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 6,
				30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 12, 181</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhŏdŏ-pēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Rhodopean</i>, for <i>Thracian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 461</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regna,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Thrace</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					347</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vates,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Orpheus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					10, 11</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also called heros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 10, 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spicula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					12, 400</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saxa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. III. Cons. Hon. 113</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flumina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. IV. Cons. Hon. 526</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjux,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Progne</i>, <i>wife of the Thracian king
						Tereus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 5, 121</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhŏdŏ-pēus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Thracian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saxa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					6, 618</span></i>
			.</div>
